1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:03,980
Every selfie you post hides
a reflection.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:07,345
Now AI can step inside your eye
and look around.

3
00:00:07,505 --> 00:00:13,185
Across healthy adults, the human cornea
curves like a 7.8 mm dome,

4
00:00:13,185 --> 00:00:15,821
acting as a tiny wide-angle
security mirror.

5
00:00:15,981 --> 00:00:20,141
At the University of Maryland,
researchers fed portrait clips

6
00:00:20,141 --> 00:00:22,481
into a 3D neural radiance field.

7
00:00:22,641 --> 00:00:27,651
Previously, two things blocked this:
micro-shifts as eyeballs rotate,

8
00:00:27,651 --> 00:00:31,239
and your colored iris overpowering
faint room reflections.

9
00:00:31,399 --> 00:00:35,159
Their algorithm locks onto cornea pose
while peeling away

10
00:00:35,159 --> 00:00:37,272
a 2D map of your iris texture.

11
00:00:37,432 --> 00:00:42,302
Suddenly, hidden rooms, plush toys,
and bystanders appear in 3D,

12
00:00:42,302 --> 00:00:44,793
given enough head motion.

13
00:00:44,953 --> 00:00:49,165
Then they tested public music videos
of Miley Cyrus and Lady Gaga...

14
00:00:49,805 --> 00:00:54,185
Zooming into single eyes, phantom
silhouettes of studio lights

15
00:00:54,185 --> 00:00:56,855
and camera crews emerged years later.

16
00:00:56,855 --> 00:00:57,436
Remember...
